  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In acidic medium, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></math> shows oxidising action as represented in the half reaction</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>XH</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>Ye</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>→</mo><mn>2</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ZH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> are respectively are:</p>",
    "image": null
  },
