  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Potassium dichromate, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></math>, is a common inorganic chemical reagent, most commonly used as an oxidizing agent in various laboratory and industrial applications. </p><p>The balanced reaction is,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>→</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>Cr</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math></p>",
